problem:
Expand and simplify completely: \begin{align*}
x\left(x(1+x)+2x\right)-3(x^2-x+2)
\end{align*}

target_step_text:
Next, I can distribute the -3 on the right side: \begin{align*}
-3(x^2-x+2) &= -3x^2+3x-6
\end{align*}

The final answer is the quotient plus the remainder, so I have:

# Answer

x^5 - x^4 + x^3 - x^2 + x - 1 - \frac{2}{x+1}

